{
  "experiment_id": "C001",
  "status": "prepared",
  "scope": "a functional-mechanism test, on a CPU toy task, of a learned-attention global workspace (competitive top-k write, gated slot update, broadcast read-back by every module) against parameter-matched pairwise comparators (all-to-all, bandwidth-matched and sparse top-k pairwise attention; the judged comparison) and ablations (no-broadcast, competition off, capacity off: reported attribution contrasts; no communication: floor) and crippled and weak all-to-all as gross and graded sensitivity controls: shared-weight modules, a finite training set of eight modules, evaluation on sixteen modules (primary) and twenty-four (secondary) with more distractors; the primary endpoint is accuracy on sixteen modules, judged by one-sided 95% t bounds over twenty seeds of the paired difference. It does not test the deterministic ptr-pods::workspace contract, and it makes no claim about consciousness",
